    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d239">

                <pb facs="0345" n="277" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg277"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72112/976½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-03-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">19 March, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I am sending you
                    herewith an outline sketch of the substance of a reply to the British
                        note<anchor n="51" xml:id="d239-f1"/> which accompanied the recent Order in
                    Council.</p>
                <p>It is intended as a suggestion, and as the basis upon which we may be shaping our
                    thoughts in this important matter. You will see that <pb facs="0346" n="278"
                        xml:id="pg278"/> what I have done is little more than to reduce to writing
                    what I roughly indicated in Cabinet to-day.</p>
                <p>Faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Woodrow Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d239-a1.xml" xpointer="d239-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d239-f1" n="51" xml:id="d239-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 1798 from the Ambassador in Great Britain, <ref
                        target="frus1915Supp#pg_143">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1915, supp., p.
                    143</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
